      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion Juan. I\u0027d like to keep enter/exit convention here.\n\nWe need this because operations like `fork()`, cross-process syscalls, or kernel threads (`kswapd`) work on a remote mm whose page size might differ from current-\u003emm.\n\n`P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM(mm)` uses `\u003clinux/cleanup.h\u003e` to temporarily bind the target mm and auto-restore it on scope exit.\n\nI went with enter/exit because it acts as the constructor/destructor for entering a temporary execution context",
      "parentUuid": "bb01d0a4_296dea0a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 32,
